- From `Owner`: `address` `@NotEmpty`; `city` `@NotEmpty`; `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be in E.164 form")`
- `email`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode` — no constraints
- `pets` — `@OneToMany(cascade = ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = EAGER)`

Lifecycle callback (side-effect at persist time), lines 79-84:

```java
@PrePersist
void defaultRegistrationDate() {
    if (this.registrationDate == null) {
        this.registrationDate = LocalDate.now();
    }
}
```

So if no `registrationDate` is supplied, it defaults to the server's current date at persist time.

